{
  "description" : "docs/contracts/i18n.md sections 2 to 4. 'layers' are two layers of catalogs (language tag to the catalog file's JSON), the base first; 'lookup' cases give the bundle's text for (locale, key, args); 'format' cases are the placeholder rules alone; 'placeholders' the names a text contains; 'plurals' the CLDR category of a count (plain decimal text) for a language; 'resolve' the locale chosen for a supported list, a user preference, a tenant default and an Accept-Language header; 'validation' the text of a field error.",
  "howToRun" : "Parse each layer's catalogs (messages are strings or plural objects with 'other'), build a bundle of the layers (later layers win within one tag; per key the tag, then its language, then en). For each case compute the 'expect' and compare it exactly. Args are JSON strings or numbers; a number is the text it was written with. A key no catalog has renders as the key. Locale tags are normalised (af-za is af-ZA).",
